# I use PC shutdown to notify me that it is a time to take a break/finish the
# work for the day.
#
# Advantages:
#      1. I have to stop what I was doing.
#
#	   I could use alarm, but my issue with alarms was, that alarms can go
#	   unnoticed (e.g. if sound is muted) and are easy to postpone.
#	   Postponing is however not a good practice for building strong habits.
#	   If I need to finish some work, I can turn the PC back on for a minute
#	   (shutdown uses "+1m" as the default time parameter), which is enough
#	   time to finish my work and save files.
#
#      2. I don't have to think about turning off the PC and can just always
#      leave it on.
#
#      3. It forces me to context switch, by closing all my open apps (my
#      desktop is then less cluttered during the day) and helps me to
#      reevaluate my priorities for the day during breaks (it takes me at least
#      15min to "unfocus" from the thing I was doing until I am able to do some
#      planning). I.e. it helps me to distinguish between important and "nice to
#      have" tasks by giving me some perspective and time to do/reevaluate my
#      daily/weekly planning.
#
#      4. Optionally I can also add alarm on my phone for 10 minutes before the
#      shutdown timer, so that I am not surprised by the shutdown.
#
#      TODO - what if I will be having an online call or teaching? TOSOLVE

*      0-7    * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
0-15   9      * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
45-59  11     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
*      12     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
30-59  15     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
15-59  19     * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
*      20-23  * * *  root /sbin/shutdown
